     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 1,700 mg is also well above the usual maximum single dose of about 850 mg to 1,000 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nWas a different dose meant? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily.** These are common regimens.\n- **1,700 mg total per day.** If so, it would need to be split, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me that and add a clinical justification. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
